WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.980
<i>Present day 
High-school student Saburo</i>

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:11.080
<i>finds himself taken back in time 
to the Warring States period.</i>

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:18.880
Horse!

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.330
Ah, there...

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:25.750
You... you look like...

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.450
Oh, yeah!

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.150
You look like me!

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.470
I ask you to use your manly face

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.200
to be my decoy!

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:39.440
<i>And he came to live 
as Nobunaga Oda.</i>

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.180
Huh?

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.030
<b>Episode 2</b>

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.030
<b>Kanshi</b>

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.760
Soon after slipping back to 
the Warring States period,

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.210
Saburo became the successor 
to the Oda family.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:05.660
But...

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.810
...with his reputation for being a fool,
 Saburo caused much unrest.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:15.670
Owari experienced riot after riot.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.340
Is this a historical drama?

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:24.590
My lord!

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.260
Follow the lord!

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:37.360
Saburo himself led his army 
in an honest effort

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.840
to quell the various uprisings.

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:43.250
My lord!

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.250
My lord!

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:49.410
Tsuneoki, I haven't seen our lord.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:54.410
Yes... well... 
he is out with our mistress.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:56.820
On another so-called "date"?

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:00.440
Yes. A "date" thing.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.060
What is that man doing?

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.560
He is our family leader now.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:11.770
That is why, to this day, 
people still rebel against our lord.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:26.180
It is quite lively.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:27.250
Yeah.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.490
I told you we'd be better off 
without those checking stations.

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:30.560
Yes!

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:36.450
It's true that with the checking stations eliminated 
and the state borders opened,

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:40.180
people may gather, and Owari 
may become even more affluent.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.550
Right!

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:47.430
But it also means that 
spies and assassins

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:51.990
can enter from other 
states more easily.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.230
I suppose.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.360
And at such a time,

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.650
when we must strengthen 
protection around our lord,

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.340
he is one on of his "dates"!

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:06.620
But our lord has grand ambitions.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.670
He will surely accomplish something great!

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.830
I truly believe it.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:17.930
You seem to understand our lord well.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:22.680
Yes! Because I am young, 
I am quick to adapt.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.800
I would not be able to keep up 
with our lord otherwise.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.950
And I suppose I am 
but a stubborn old git?

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.110
Yes!

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.300
What?!

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.730
Everyone, come see this!

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:34.520
What?

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.890
He has a spear!

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:35.890
A fight?

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:38.400
Please, not in front of my shop.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.880
I never asked for a fight.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:44.970
No, but you bumped into 
me deliberately.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.900
<i>You</i> bumped into me deliberately!

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:54.250
Well, it does not matter
who bumped into whom first.

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:57.590
There is but one way to settle this.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:03.090
With a test of our skills!

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.710
No fighting!

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.270
Who are you?

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:34.260
My lord!

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.370
Lord — what?

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:38.110
Nobunaga?

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:42.090
My name is Inuchiyo Maeda.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.570
Inuchiyo?

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.610
I have long admired you,

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:50.350
and have wanted to serve you!

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:53.350
Inu (Dog)?

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:57.700
Woof!

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:00.150
Woof!

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.350
You're hired!

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:02.970
I like your response.

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:03.530
Huh?

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.320
You will hire me?

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:06.860
Yup.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.870
I like your name, Inuchiyo.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:13.980
I will put my life 
on the line for you.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.970
So? What about you, mister?

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.020
I am Narimasa Sassa.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:26.300
I, too, have dreamed of 
serving you —

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.170
Hired!

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:27.760
Huh?

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.620
My lord, you're being so hasty again.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.340
Well, they look tough.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:38.310
I thank you for your kind words!

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:40.530
I'm hungry.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:41.480
Let's go.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.610
So it is true that the lord 
will hire you if he likes you.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:59.150
Perhaps he would hire us, too,
 if we did the same.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.880
So that is Nobunaga Oda.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:15.310
I have heard, my lord,

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:20.490
that you hired more sketchy men.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:22.600
I hired them because 
they're really lively.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:26.880
Well, I beg you not to 
hire people needlessly.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:28.970
Some of them may have 
disagreeable motives.

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:31.330
Don't say that!

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:33.060
They're all good people.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:34.940
I think.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.160
I don't know them too well.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.910
That is so sloppy.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:41.920
How could I take over Japan 
being so picky?

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:45.090
Take over Japan?

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:47.840
Again, with such hubris.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:52.050
It's Nobunaga's calling 
to take over Japan.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:14.530
What are you thinking, Hirate-dono, 
gathering so shady people many here?

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:17.070
<i>Katsuie Shibata.</i>

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:20.710
<i>Chief retainer to the Oda family, 
and its strongest general.</i>

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:23.010
I did not gather them.

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:25.980
They came on their own.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.500
And what do you plan 
to do with them?

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.680
We have no choice 
but to interview them.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:36.060
It is the most that an old one 
such as myself can do.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:47.730
Next, come forth!

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:48.900
Yes, sir!

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:54.860
I am Yoshinari Mori.

00:07:55.130 --> 00:08:00.000
Nobunaga-sama is soon to 
become a great general.

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:05.570
I have come eagerly to 
fight for Nobunaga-sama.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:08.510
Father, godspeed!

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:11.510
I want to serve, too.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:14.470
But you are still a child, Brother.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:15.950
Shut up, Ranmaru.

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:17.500
Like you're one to talk!

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:22.570
You're hired.

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:24.520
Work hard for our lord.

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:25.610
Yes, sir!

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.360
All right!

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:33.340
All right, all right!

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.070
Next person, come forth.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:39.510
Hello.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:44.670
Your name?

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.700
Denjirou Tahara is the name.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:50.240
I work in my family's merchant business.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.900
Son of tradesfolk, you say.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:52.900
Yes.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:58.920
I had heard that the lord here allows 
people of all standings to serve.

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:03.350
I'm sorry, but I will be 
unable to hire you.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:09.760
You are not fit to be a samurai.

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:13.900
Now leave Owari immediately!

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.600
Should I risk it?

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:27.790
<b>Baby Star Ramen</b>

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:24.130
It's...

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:27.790
...not spoiled, is it?

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.680
The expiration date...

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:35.920
...is really far away.

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:52.050
It's good!

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:55.150
Want some?

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:56.520
It's good.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:04.160
My lord, just what is that?

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:06.240
Huh? Baby Star.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:09.090
Baby... Star?

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.200
Yeah.

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:11.450
Want some?

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.450
N-No, thank you.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:16.210
Why not?

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:21.040
You might never get 
another chance to!

00:10:28.610 --> 00:10:30.570
How salty!

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:35.930
Yet such indescribable flavor 
fills my mouth!

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:38.600
It would go well with white rice!

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:40.320
You sound like a 
gourmet food critic.

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.740
Gourmet?

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:45.990
Oh! Jii!

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:48.520
How were the interviews?

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:50.350
Any lively ones?

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:52.170
Indeed.

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.500
Thanks for your hard work.

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:59.490
Here, have some, and relax.

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.740
Thank you.

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:15.850
What is the matter, Hirate-sama?

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:17.920
My teeth...

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:19.240
Teeth?

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:25.120
It is too hard for an 
old man such as myself.

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:26.660
I am sorry.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:37.330
Old as he may be, he is still 
an Oda family chief retainer.

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:39.560
So Hirate saw through you.

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:40.780
Yeah.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.640
He figured me out right away.

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:47.250
And you? How was Sunpu?

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:51.400
We are well on our way 
to entering.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:54.310
Now we simply wait 
for the right time.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:12:01.550
Sir Yoshimoto eagerly 
awaits your report.

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:19.010
Such a pest, that old man.

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:22.730
How can this be?

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:28.440
It was the lord himself who 
asked to see his new servants.

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:31.480
Yet he is absent.

00:12:31.990 --> 00:12:36.500
Is he on yet another "date"?

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:41.690
I am pleased that he is well,

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:45.820
but if he strays too far, his subordinates 
will not follow his leadership.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:50.510
<i>Oda resident scholar, 
Niwa Nagahide.</i>

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:54.630
The lord must have 
something in mind.

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:58.010
Is that not true, Hirate-dono?

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:02.340
I do not know what 
he thinks either.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:02.800
What?

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:09.780
But the lord is certainly not a fool.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.430
He is simply...

00:13:13.150 --> 00:13:16.730
...beyond our comprehension.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:20.480
And yet everyone calls him a fool.

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:29.490
That is what frustrates me.

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:38.920
It's cooled!

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.460
Energy charge!

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:52.910
My lord, you have 
many strange things.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:55.790
I thought I'd give this to Jii.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:59.400
He can drink it, 
even with his bad teeth.

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:02.990
You are so kind, my lord.

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:12.940
Hirate!

00:14:14.530 --> 00:14:16.290
Hirate!

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.620
Huh? Where's Hirate?

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:22.780
Hirate-dono went home 
not long ago.

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:26.400
Oh, I see...

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:33.600
Isn't this his fan?

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.310
He must have forgotten it.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.810
Shall I have our men deliver it?

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:41.010
No. I'll go.

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:42.490
There's something I want 
to give him anyway.

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:43.690
See you soon.

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:45.710
My lord!

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:07.250
Hirate's mansion was 
this way, wasn't it?

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:48.480
Hirate!

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:54.140
Hirate!

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:57.280
Hirate!

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:01.290
Hirate!

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:03.020
My lord!

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:07.280
Who did this?

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:08.620
Call an ambulance!

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.570
My lord,

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:17.360
there is an assassin 
after your life.

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:22.160
Return quickly to the castle.

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:24.680
Hirate, stop talking!

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:27.010
You'll bleed out!

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:28.880
This is...

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:32.240
...the last time...

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:35.590
...I shall lecture you.

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.440
I got it.

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:42.480
Please, stop talking.

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:44.250
My lord,

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:48.880
live as you please.

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:54.970
And let everyone see

00:16:55.810 --> 00:17:00.020
what only you can see.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:04.690
My lord...

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:09.130
Hirate! Hirate!

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:15.870
Rule the land.

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:20.510
So that none

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:28.540
will ever call you a fool.

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:33.610
Rule.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:58.340
Saburo announced Hirate's 
death as a <i>kanshi.</i>

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:05.130
<i>Kanshi</i> is to commit suicide

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:07.870
to admonish a master for his actions.

00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:24.740
I have received word that 
Hirate-dono has committed <i>kanshi</i>.

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:29.980
He did not need to kill himself for it.

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:32.220
He had become disheartened

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:38.300
by Nobunaga-dono's
ceaseless riotous behavior.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:56.820
Our lord...

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:00.260
On such a rainy day.

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:06.750
Hirate-sama's...

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:11.940
Hirate's suicide will not 
cure our lord's foolishness.

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:12.520
Yeah.

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:14.590
Back to work!

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:15.780
Yes, sir!

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:21.810
My lord...

00:19:27.360 --> 00:19:28.980
Oh?

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:31.370
You were a farmer, you say.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:32.410
Yeah.

00:19:32.410 --> 00:19:36.300
But I thought I was better 
suited to be a merchant.

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:38.460
So I sell needles now.

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:39.830
Your name?

00:19:40.430 --> 00:19:42.360
What do you go by?

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:45.620
Toukichiro Kinoshita.

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:49.240
Toukichiro.

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:51.500
That is a good name.

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:53.890
Not really.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:57.060
No! I like it.

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:02.770
In fact, I want it.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:26.040
<i>Had I been mistaken?</i>

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:56.770
Needles!

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.190
Buy your needles!

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:04.730
Strong and durable, 
Toukichiro's needles!

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:07.100
Buy your needles!

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:11.870
Strong and durable, 
Toukichiro's needles!

00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:13.440
Buy your needles!

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:15.720
I'll have one.

00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:21.250
Thank you!
